 LYcVqQOUBbRasHkVB9KNl83rbiGw/viewform?usp=header\n\nNo Ideas But in Things
 \n\nFilmed and Directed by Lan A. Li\nProduced by Peter N. Miller\n\nShort
  Film Screening\,\nfollowed by a discussion with the filmmakers\n\n"No Ide
 as But in Things" is an art film that asks what can only be known through 
 touch\, making\, and the body. Drawing on footage from the Material Intell
 igence seminar at the American Academy in Rome\, where scientists\, makers
 \, and humanists explored how to learn from materials in an age of words a
 nd algorithms\, the film uses Rome as an object of inquiry and conversatio
 n as an instrument of research\, rather than a vehicle for predetermined c
 onclusions. In doing so\, it reimagines scholarly output beyond the book\,
  article\, and essay.\n \n\nNovember 5\, 4:30-6PM (Clark Center Auditorium
 )
